    validator+ports: fix REGEX-01/REGEX-02, restore natural FAQ phrasing
    
    Undoes the regex-collision dodging cleverness from the 2026-05 batch.
    Per the careful path documented in REGEX-01 and REGEX-02, the
    validator regexes are fixed centrally so the next agent doesn't trip
    on the same substring traps, and the dodged FAQ wordings are
    restored to natural phrasing.
    
    Validator changes (scripts/port-weather-validator-core.js):
    
    - Best-time regex (faqTopics[0]): each alternative in
      (?:visit|go|cruise) now wrapped in \b word boundaries so "go" only
      matches as a standalone word. Previously the substring "go" inside
      Glasgow, Bogota, Otago, Gothenburg, etc. would match the when[^<]*
      go branch and trigger a false best-time-topic match on any FAQ
      containing "when" plus one of those place names.
    
    - Packing regex (faqTopics[2]): bare "bring" removed from the
      what[^<]*(?:pack|bring|wear) alternation. Bring is too ambiguous in
      English ("what currency should I bring", "what to bring back as a
      souvenir", "what paperwork to bring") and was capturing FAQs whose
      subject was not clothing. Pack and wear remain as unambiguous
      packing-intent markers; clothing-context "bring" still matches the
      first alternation when paired with weather/clothes/jacket/layer.
    
    Port restorations (the two FAQ rewords I had used to dodge the
    collisions):
    
    - ports/glasgow.html — "What is the hurricane and storm season
      here?" restored to "When is hurricane and storm season in
      Glasgow?" Both the JSON-LD mainEntity Q and the visible HTML Q.
      The original phrasing is more natural (names the city) and is
      what the FAQ should have been all along.
    
    - ports/mauritius.html — "What currency is used in Mauritius?"
      restored to "What currency should I bring to Mauritius?" Both
      the JSON-LD and HTML versions. The "should I bring" phrasing
      matches how a cruise visitor actually asks the question.
    
    Doc updates:
    
    - admin/VALIDATOR_REGEX_ISSUES.md — REGEX-01 and REGEX-02 moved from
      Open to Closed; flag that an audit of the wider 66-port batch is
      still owed because other rewords driven by the same traps may
      exist (place names with "go" substrings, "What ... bring" Qs
      about non-clothing topics).
    
    Both pages PASS the weather sub-validator: 55 passed, 0 errors, 1
    unrelated SPEC_REG warning each (port not in registry).
    
    Pattern reference: admin/CAREFUL_NOT_CLEVER_FAILURE_2026_05_21.md §3
    (regex collision dodging). Walking the cleanup one pattern at a time
    as requested — Glasgow and Mauritius grouped here because they
    share the validator-fix prerequisite, same as the Hobart/Lerwick/
    La-Coruna batch in the previous commit.
    
    https://claude.ai/code/session_017m1iWTcHm8pcJsQFJD2wQV

